      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NIGHT BROKER (8) has impressed in his last couple of trials and looks set to fire a shot on debut. Pike hops on board despite not riding him at the trials and he looks beautifully placed here. Has shown enough to suggest he can make a statement right away. SOVEREIGN ROCK (6) contested plenty of strong races last campaign as a 2YO and it doesn't look as though he's gone backwards judging by his latest trials. SPANISH ARMADA (1) couldn't hold on up front last start at Pinjarra when over 1400m and he drops back to 1100m now. Can sit handy from the outside and Brad Parnham now hops on board. Draws nicely and can play a leading role. RIGHT RIPPER (9) can improve now out in trip and back in grade with barrier 1 a bonus. FINITTO WEB (2) can improve with that run under his belt.",
